# KDE Plasma 6 Wayland Suite — Cursor CLI & Agent Rule

This rule enables Cursor (GUI and Cursor CLI / `cursor-agent`) to diagnose and execute KDE Plasma 6 Wayland automations.

## Available Commands via CLI

```bash
# Health diagnostic of the environment
./bin/kde-config status

# Set user language preference (en / pt-BR)
./bin/kde-config set-lang [en|pt-BR]

# Shortcuts (Ctrl+<key>), native cedilla, and clipboard
./bin/kde-config fix-keyboard

# Unlock keyboard matrix on Tongfang/Avell laptops via GRUB
./bin/kde-config fix-tongfang

# Dynamic keyboard power management (anti-latch + battery saver)
./bin/kde-config smart-keyboard-power --apply

# Configure and audit AI host profile and model role map
./bin/kde-config configure-harness

# Touchpad gestures (libinput-gestures)
./bin/kde-config gestures

# Logitech MX Master 3S (logiops)
./bin/kde-config mouse

# Battery / power — diagnostic (read-only)
./bin/kde-config battery-status

# Battery / power — apply/revert fixes
BATTERY_FIX_GPU_PRIMARY=1 ./bin/kde-config battery-apply
./bin/kde-config battery-revert

# Analytical run report with interactive selection and recommendations
./bin/kde-config report
./bin/kde-config report --list

# Help Center
./bin/kde-config help

# Switch active layout via D-Bus
./bin/kde-config switch [br|us]
```

## Execution Architecture & Discipline (See `skills/kde-wayland-suite-architecture`)

- Canonical script source is `base/shared/`; command source is `base/commands/`.
- Platform directories (`claude-code/`, `omp/`, `cursor/`, `opencode/`, `antigravity/`, `commands/`, `shared/`, `bin/`) are compatibility symlinks.
- Every command must follow `base/shared/OUTPUT-CONTRACT.md`: **Plan** → **Execution** → **Summary** → **Recommended Actions**.
- Internal commands and contracts are strictly in English; user-facing responses are translated to the user's selected language (e.g. `pt-BR`) as needed.
